206:## Context ingestion
207-
208:Ingestion adapters normalize host-agent events into `NewContextItem`:
209-
210-```typescript
211-export interface NewContextItem {
212-  id: string;
213-  type: ContextType;
214-  content: string;
215-  tokenCount?: number;
216-  metadata: Partial<ContextMetadata> & Pick<ContextMetadata, "source">;
217-  tags?: readonly string[];
218-}
219-```
220-
221-Rules:
222-
223-- Preserve source and creation time when supplied by the host; otherwise use an injected clock.
224-- Normalize metadata to the Context Model shape: default `priority` to the type baseline (or neutral baseline if unknown), `ageTurns`/`references` to `0`, and `compressed`/`transformed`/`pinned` to `false`.
225-- Deduplicate by stable `id`; duplicate `add()` is an error, not an implicit update.
226-- Validate content and metadata size before storing.
227-- Do not assume the inventory should ingest every transcript/tool event. Source adapters apply collection policy.
228-- Pinned state is metadata for display; enforcement belongs to the Governor's policy layer.
229-
230-## Token estimation
231-
232-Token estimation is injected rather than hardcoded into the inventory:
233-
234-```typescript
235-export interface TokenEstimator {
236-  estimate(text: string, context?: { modelId?: string; encodingId?: string }): number;
237-}
238-```
239-
240-The selected estimator and version should be recorded with evaluation data. If a target tokenizer is available, use it; otherwise use a document

